Open items. ROADMAP.md's are done; what emberx still works around in Ember, and asks of it
upstream, is in CONTRIBUTING.md.

- @emberx/cli.
- scripts/lib/chrome-bench.js: review it.
- Find a solution for "npm run clean", "npm run dev", "npm run test:doctests" (later).
- Router: a rootURL, for an app served under a sub-path (location-bar's `root` option), which
  Router.visit() and LinkTo's hrefs would then add and strip.
- Router: model hooks that run again when a redirect starts in the middle of another transition.
- Route: buildRouteInfoMetadata, for <head> beyond the title, which `static title` covers.
- @emberx/rsvp? The rsvp npm package is probably enough: RSVP.hash() in a model hook works as it is.
